9927de4e422b39ea4141b","node_id":"C_kwDOIm6-JtoAKDc1ZDAyNjExOTM0NDk4NGUxMmY5OTI3ZGU0ZTQyMmIzOWVhNDE0MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/commit/e0061e2fb4d0515128855460d31a0404ca20a411","sha":"e0061e2fb4d0515128855460d31a0404ca20a411","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/commits/e0061e2fb4d0515128855460d31a0404ca20a411"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/commit/ade65cdc31683dce82fe8b3b12c21096496ac25e","sha":"ade65cdc31683dce82fe8b3b12c21096496ac25e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/commits/ade65cdc31683dce82fe8b3b12c21096496ac25e"}],"sha":"75d026119344984e12f9927de4e422b39ea4141b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/commits/75d026119344984e12f9927de4e422b39ea4141b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12491991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cdfarkas","id":12491991,"login":"cdfarkas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDkxOTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/commits/ade65cdc31683dce82fe8b3b12c21096496ac25e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T08:40:02Z","email":"clement.farkas@stonal.com","name":"cdfarkas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T08:44:09Z","email":"clement.farkas@stonal.com","name":"cdfarkas"},"message":"feat: rewrite the profile README and add five technical write-ups\n\n## Context\n\nThe profile was a wall of roughly fifty shields.io badges. Everyone has React, Git and VS Code, so it signalled familiarity with logos rather than anything built. The only substantive content, what I am working on and how to reach me, sat inside an HTML comment and was therefore invisible. Nothing stated the actual positioning, and nothing backed it: one public repository, zero pinned, every piece of real work in a private repo. A visitor had no way to judge any claim on the page.\n\n## Analysis\n\nCut the badge wall to seven, kept as a visual accent under a stack written in prose, because prose gets read and a logo grid does not. Brought the hidden content back into the open and kept the Portal line as a footer signature so the personality survives.\n\nThe write-ups are the evidence the page was missing. Two reviewers went over the drafts against the source notes and the real code and returned 48 findings, 10 of them blocking, and the corrections changed conclusions rather than prose. The subpath article had its central rule inverted: the variable is share-scope membership, not package ownership, so a third-party subpath duplicates exactly like a first-party one. The prefix-share explanation was folklore and now describes what the mechanism actually does. The bundler article attributed Node''s silence to the wrong mechanism and drew an invariant the incident does not support. The token-cost article was the worst: its own arithmetic shows the two marathon sessions hold 54 percent of all turns, so they dominate spend because they hold most of the work, and the recommended fix is worth about 20 percent per turn rather than the 86.8 percent the framing implied. It now publishes as a correction of its own conclusion. The migration article claimed a finished platform after a year, against 8 of 13 apps absorbed over three months.\n\nEverything is anonymised: no employer, product, application, ticket or internal library name, and no third-party stack name that would act as a fingerprint. Component examples use neutral names.\n\nThey live in this repository rather than a dedicated one so the links stay relative and nothing has to be kept in sync. Extracting them later is trivial if the corpus grows enough to deserve its own identity.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Replace the badge wall with a prose stack plus seven badges\n- Surface the previously commented-out content and add positioning, work areas and working principles\n- Add five write-ups under notes/ with an index, linked from a Writing section","tree":{"sha":"b31984f42b8e8e35afdf73959be18921da39d8cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/git/trees/b31984f42b8e8e35afdf73959be18921da39d8cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdfarkas/cdfarkas/git/commits/ade65cdc31683dce82fe8b3b12c21096496ac25e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12491991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cdfarkas","id":12491991,"login":"cdfarkas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDkxOTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdfarkas","user_view_type"